text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:10037\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1949-02-16/pdf/FR-1949-02-16.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 957b9dde9cfd9acd1ac9b52b6a3a5d8c898bab6f71c368d4fb03a71bfaf5eabe\nLocation: 14 FR 679, PDF pages 1-2 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 12 ===\nVOLUME 14 T?, 1934  ¿y4 ^A/ITED ^ NUMBER 31\nWashington, Wednesday, February 16, 1949\nTITLE 3— THE PRESIDENT  \nPROCLAMATION 2827  \nR ed C ross  M o nth, 1949\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES \nOF AM ERICA \nA PROCLAMATION\nWHEREAS the American National \nRed Cross serves as a medium through \nwhich the people of this Nation can par­\nticipate effectively in the alleviation of \nhuman suffering whenever and where- \never disaster strikes; and \nWHEREAS, specifically, the Red Cross \nexpended $12,000,000 during the last \nfiscal year in helping 312,000 individuals \nwhose communities had been ravaged by \nfloods, fires, tornadoes, or other dis­\nasters; and\nWHEREAS the Red Cross stands at \nthe side of our troops wherever they are \nstationed throughout the world, and also \nprovides invaluable assistance to those \nwar veterans who are still disabled or \nare maladjusted to civilian life; and \nWHEREAS, in order to help meet a \ngrowing post-war need, which would be \nmultiplied in the event of a national \ne","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10037.txt","sha256":"6f541f782aeb640848ca67ea1cd0adedc983d57059441f8893360b490577fb7a","source":{"line":535,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"0aae81755039605843ad81057f43373067a518af93126ac0c65f53f36a33bcf5"}}]}
